(borge-bug (id "BORGE-1783431485")
  (title "Reader escape handler bug + CRUD list/rows naming")
  (status triage)
  (created 2026-07-07)
  (filed-by roerick)
  (doc "Two findings from iteration-13 CRUD primitive work, filed together because the second surfaced while debugging the first.

(1) Reader escape handler bug (lisp/lib/reader.ml): when read_string peeked a '\\\\', it then called (match advance st with Some 'n' -> ...). But advance returns the char it CONSUMED (which was the '\\\\' we just peeked), so the match arm for Some '\\\\' fired, adding a backslash to buf — leaving the NEXT char (the actual escape letter, e.g. '\"') as the new peek. The '\"' then matched the close-quote arm, ending the string early. Result: a lisp string literal like \"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"alice\\\"}\" (which should read back as {name:alice as JSON) failed with 'trailing input after expression (col 5)' — the buf trimmed to '{\\' and everything after was leftover. Fixed by changing the escape arm to: ignore (advance st) (consume the '\\\\'), then match (peek st) against the escape letters, advancing each consumption manually. Verified by a new alcotest case in image/test/primitives_test.ml that asserts a JSON-form string roundtrips to the raw JSON string value.

(2) CRUD prim name '(list 'type)' collided with the pure list-constructor prim '(list 1 2 3)' — both were registered as 'list' and the later registration (CRUD) won, breaking primitives_test cases. Renamed CRUD's list-rows primitive to 'rows' (read as: '(rows 'type [limit])'). The spec text in [storage.types] / [lisp-interpreter.primitives] doesn't explicitly name the list-rows prim, so this is a v1 implementation choice; the spec should reflect '(rows ...)' rather than '(list ...)' when these sections are next updated in a plan pass.

CRUD primitives on the Lwt-typed ABI (it12 refactor) are now fully functional: (get 'type id), (create 'type fields), (update 'type id fields), (delete 'type id), (rows 'type [limit]). Each returns its real DB result through the promise chain — '(define u (get 'user id))' then '(str u)' returns the row's fields, proving the read-side composition that the it12 ABI refactor was built to enable. Smoke test: /tmp/pp_crud_it13.py.")
)
